This file is a placeholder. No license has been finalized for this
repository yet. Until this file is replaced with actual license text,
treat this specification as "all rights reserved" / internal use only —
do not redistribute or build on it outside channels your team has
explicitly approved.

Things to decide before replacing this file:

1. License model
   - Open-source, permissive (Apache-2.0, MIT, ...)
   - Open-source, copyleft (GPL-family) — unusual for an API spec, but an
     option
   - Proprietary grant scoped to named internal teams
   - Proprietary grant scoped to named external partners (e.g. under an
     existing NDA/partnership agreement)

2. Scope of the grant
   - Who may read this spec vs. who may build an adapter/controller
     against it vs. who may redistribute it further
   - Whether the grant covers the .proto files only, or also any
     generated client/server stub code produced from them

3. Patent considerations
   - Whether any grant should include an explicit patent license/covenant
     (common in Apache-2.0-style licenses; relevant if this HAL design or
     any device-adapter pattern here is separately patented)

4. Attribution requirements
   - Whether integrators must retain a notice, credit Cisco, or similar

5. Warranty / liability disclaimer
   - Standard "AS IS, NO WARRANTY" language, or something specific to
     hardware-control use (given this spec governs lab hardware, consider
     whether any liability language around physical safety is warranted)

Common starting points if going the open-source route:
  https://choosealicense.com/
  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
  https://opensource.org/license/mit/

Once a decision is made, replace this entire file's contents with the
actual license text and update the "License" section in README.md to
match (currently marked TBD, pointing here).
